.TH "RTCICECANDIDATE.TOJSON" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCIceCandidate.toJSON \- RTCIceCandidate: toJSON() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]toJSON()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]RTCIceCandidate\f[R] interface returns a JSON\-serializable plain
object representing the \f[CR]RTCIceCandidate\f[R] object.
.PP
The method is automatically called by \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R] when
an \f[CR]RTCIceCandidate\f[R] object is encountered during JSON
serialization.
The serialized value can then be deserialized using the
\f[CR]RTCIceCandidate()\f[R] constructor within the reviver of
\f[CR]JSON.parse()\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toJSON()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A JSON\-serializable plain object containing the following properties:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]candidate\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]sdpMid\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]sdpMLineIndex\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]usernameFragment\f[R]
.PP
Each property\(cqs value is copied as\-is.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Calling toJSON() directly
This example creates an \f[CR]RTCIceCandidate\f[R] object.
Calling \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] directly returns a plain object.
Its properties have the same values as the corresponding properties of
the original object.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] candidate = \f[B]new\f[R] RTCIceCandidate({
  candidate: \(dq\(dq,
  sdpMid: \(dq0\(dq,
  sdpMLineIndex: 0,
});

\f[B]const\f[R] json = candidate.toJSON();
console.log(json); \f[I]// A plain object\f[R]
console.log(\f[B]typeof\f[R] json); \f[I]// \(dqobject\(dq\f[R]
console.log(json.candidate); \f[I]// Same value as candidate.candidate\f[R]
.EE
.SS Serializing to a JSON string
The \f[CR]RTCIceCandidate\f[R] object from the previous example is
serialized using \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R], which calls the
\f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] method automatically.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] jsonString = JSON.stringify(candidate);
console.log(jsonString);
.EE
.PP
This would log a JSON string like so (formatted for readability):
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqcandidate\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
  \(dqsdpMid\(dq: \(dq0\(dq,
  \(dqsdpMLineIndex\(dq: 0,
  \(dqusernameFragment\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R]
}
.EE
